   "screen": "Recap: the creative design process",
   "title": "Figure 1.1.1 · The seven-stage creative design process",
   "alt": "A vertical flowchart of seven numbered stages: 1 Acceptance, commit to the task and identify the time, energy, resources and responsibility needed; 2 Analysis, research the idea and its market and speak to the people it will help; 3 Definition, restate the problem as a clear goal and set the scope; 4 Ideation, brainstorm and log every idea; 5 Selection, choose the idea that best meets the objectives; 6 Implementation, sequence the tasks in a Gantt chart and execute them; 7 Evaluation, gather feedback and decide what to improve. A dashed arrow loops from Evaluation back to Implementation, labelled fix.",
   "caption": "The stages run in order from Acceptance to Evaluation, and each one should be documented for your SBA. Notice the dashed loop: evaluation feedback sends you back to fix the product before launch.",
