   "title": "Figure 1.7.3 · Keyframes and a tween on a timeline",
   "alt": "Top: a stage showing a ball at frame 1 on the left and at frame 24 on the right, with dashed ghost circles between them, labelled software calculates the inbetweens. Bottom: a timeline with frame numbers 1 to 24 and two layers. The Ball layer has a filled keyframe dot at frame 1 and at frame 24, with a shaded Classic Tween span and an arrow between them. The Background layer has a keyframe at frame 1 and its frames extended to frame 24. A red playhead line sits at frame 12. Legend: filled dot, keyframe, F6; hollow dot, blank keyframe, F7; F5 inserts frames and extends a hold. Footnote: 24 frames played at 24 fps equals 1 second; more frames at the same rate give a longer, slower action.",
   "caption": "You set only the two keyframes; the tween fills frames 2 to 23. Add easing in the Properties panel so the motion does not look mechanical.",
