   "screen": "The design journey: from concept to interactive experience",
   "title": "Figure 2.3.1 · The design journey: wireframe, mockup, prototype",
   "alt": "Three phone screens joined by arrows. 1 Wireframe: grey boxes, an image placeholder crossed with an X, lines for text and an outlined Book button; structure and layout, low fidelity, greyscale. 2 Mockup: the same layout with a coloured header, a picture, the title Bay Street Café and a solid Book button; look and feel with colours, fonts and images, but static. 3 Prototype: the mockup with a tap ripple on the Book button and an arrow to the next screen, labelled tap; clickable, it tests interactions and flow. An arrow underneath shows fidelity, detail and time increasing from left to right.",
   "caption": "Each stage builds on the last. Fix structure while it is cheap grey boxes; add colour only once the layout works; then link screens to test the flow.",
