   "screen": "What is mobile user experience?",
   "title": "Figure 3.5.1 · Seven UX factors in one moment: Maria at a bus stop",
   "alt": "A flat illustration of Maria, a nurse, standing at a bus stop with a phone, under a bright sun, with a car passing and noise lines, a nearly empty battery icon and low signal bars beside the phone. Seven numbered tags in the scene match seven cards. 1 Screen size: a small screen, read while standing in the street. 2 Bandwidth: only a little data left this month. 3 Portability: on the move, at a bus stop on Back Street. 4 Processing power: an older Android phone on 8% battery. 5 Accessibility: text and buttons she can read and tap easily. 6 Environment: bright sunshine and traffic noise. 7 User profile: a nurse checking her shift schedule. A box at the bottom gives the memory hook \"Small Bandits Pick Pockets And Escape Unseen\": screen, bandwidth, portability, processing power, accessibility, environment, user profile.",
   "caption": "All seven factors act on one user at the same moment. Design for people like Maria, not for yourself on a new phone and fast Wi-Fi.",
