   "screen": "Super apps and the consolidation of services",
   "title": "Figure 3.9.3 · A super app: many services, one login and one wallet",
   "alt": "Left: a phone running TT One, a super app idea for Trinidad and Tobago, with a wallet at its centre and the words one login, one wallet. Six services radiate from it: bus times, power bill payment, food delivery, event tickets, messaging and shopping. Right, benefits: one login and one wallet; small businesses reach many users; it saves storage and data; built-in wallets can include the unbanked. Concerns: one company holds huge amounts of data; developers depend on its rules and fees; there is less competition for local apps; one outage or breach hits everything.",
   "caption": "WeChat and Grab grew this way, adding services around a core app and a wallet. A \"discuss\" answer needs both boxes and a balanced judgement.",
